                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39704f2a-e6ca-31d7-9398-927ddc2ba02c",
                        "entry_id": "72616658-7f73-33a6-8411-c90a2f3e575c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "do granic wytrzymałości"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46a42d48-3556-418b-a544-090cf76777ce",
                                "sense_id": "39704f2a-e6ca-31d7-9398-927ddc2ba02c",
                                "text": "Przed samym wyjazdem pokłóciłem się z Pawłem o jakąś drobnostkę i wsiedliśmy do samolotu śmiertelnie na siebie obrażeni."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.3\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "681096e3-6767-421b-88b2-cbc5d0e1e2ab",
                        "source_entry_id": "72616658-7f73-33a6-8411-c90a2f3e575c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0b795fc4-5443-3969-9830-64c1cc0bafd5",
                        "target_lang_word": "fatally",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fatally",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c478eae1-28e3-391b-9177-c6f64a83158d",
                                        "entry_id": "944776c0-2fba-3bfd-98d9-eb62d84604ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a deadly manner; lethally."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94ef960d-3398-4dcb-97fd-45d514aea20a",
                                                "sense_id": "c478eae1-28e3-391b-9177-c6f64a83158d",
                                                "text": "Witness our too much memorable shame\nWhen Cressy battle fatally was struck,\nAnd all our princes captiv'd by the hand\nOf that black name, Edward, Black Prince of Wales;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f6ce317-713d-4302-8382-3cfdecc72585",
                                                "sense_id": "c478eae1-28e3-391b-9177-c6f64a83158d",
                                                "text": "He told Peace that he did not believe his statement that he had fired the pistol merely to frighten the constable; had not Robinson guarded his head with his arm he would have been wounded fatally, and Peace condemned to death."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "acc7d14d-3cbe-459a-ad06-67cf046455ee",
                                                "sense_id": "c478eae1-28e3-391b-9177-c6f64a83158d",
                                                "text": "A 22-year-old man has been jailed for life with a minimum term of 25 years for fatally stabbing 22-year-old Tashan Daniel in an unprovoked attack at Hillingdon Underground station on September 24 2019."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aae1dc5e-2804-4af2-a279-55d8ffb8bf81",
                                                "sense_id": "c478eae1-28e3-391b-9177-c6f64a83158d",
                                                "text": "White, too, was found dead—fatally shot—at the scene."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6acb471b-3cb1-387d-bae7-5ccac93804b5",
                                        "entry_id": "944776c0-2fba-3bfd-98d9-eb62d84604ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ultimately, with finality or irrevocability, moving towards the demise of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08391d6d-84f9-4ddd-bd75-16eb38164a43",
                                                "sense_id": "6acb471b-3cb1-387d-bae7-5ccac93804b5",
                                                "text": "Chelsea will point to that victory margin as confirmation of their superiority - but Spurs will complain their hopes of turning the game around were damaged fatally by Atkinson's decision."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77603902-540a-4a93-8e83-47df5645006f",
                                                "sense_id": "6acb471b-3cb1-387d-bae7-5ccac93804b5",
                                                "text": "\"They pretend,\" as I hear, \"that the verses of Kabir have four different senses; illusion, spirit, intellect, and the exoteric doctrine of the Vedas;\" but in this part of the world it is considered a ground for complaint if a man's writings admit of more than one interpretation. While England endeavors to cure the potato-rot, will not any endeavor to cure the brain-rot, which prevails so much more widely and fatally?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b0116490-1d5d-3f7e-808b-3030f88b8aeb",
                                        "entry_id": "944776c0-2fba-3bfd-98d9-eb62d84604ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fatedly; according to the dictates of fate or doom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5bd52db-9bbe-4423-845d-54b21c532920",
                                                "sense_id": "b0116490-1d5d-3f7e-808b-3030f88b8aeb",
                                                "text": "He was a slender young man in hot black clothes; he wore the unfaçaded collar fatally and unanimously adopted by all adam's-apple men of morals; he was washed, fair, flat-skulled, clean-minded, and industrious; and the only noise of any kind he ever made in the world was on Sunday."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b81fe01b-ce87-49c2-aae5-00b3f5c02d79",
                        "source_entry_id": "72616658-7f73-33a6-8411-c90a2f3e575c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0b795fc4-5443-3969-9830-64c1cc0bafd5",
                        "target_lang_word": "mortally",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mortally",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fe55a93-6401-3532-8b75-16395e9a12c9",
                                        "entry_id": "d0f20034-e7eb-35a0-b209-8acb44966771",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fatally; in such a way as to cause death."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12715c77-c516-461b-8ee6-9236bed23d4f",
                                                "sense_id": "4fe55a93-6401-3532-8b75-16395e9a12c9",
                                                "text": "Sir Philip Sidney, soldier, courtier, statesman and poet, was born at Penshurst in 1554. He won imperishable fame 32 years later at the Battle of Zutphen in Holland when, mortally wounded, he refused a drink of water and passed his flask to a wounded soldier, with the words: 'Thy necessity is yet greater than mine.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6096180-15be-3cbc-86c4-0b33a27cfe1f",
                                        "entry_id": "d0f20034-e7eb-35a0-b209-8acb44966771",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "As a mortal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1a85b63-de0c-4580-beee-6e44de736de9",
                                                "sense_id": "f6096180-15be-3cbc-86c4-0b33a27cfe1f",
                                                "text": "And all the depth of rightfull doome was taught / By faire Astræa with great industrie, / Whilest here on earth she lived mortallie […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d19f1582-afb0-419d-84c1-2b2c57edce23",
                        "source_entry_id": "72616658-7f73-33a6-8411-c90a2f3e575c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0b795fc4-5443-3969-9830-64c1cc0bafd5",
